  "id": "COMPOUND:43679 - PROTEIN:4886",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Methyl(20S,25)-Epoxy-24Alpha-Hydroxy-3,4-Secodammar-4(28)-En-3-Oate interacts with Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR. This compound appears to act as a target of multiple secondary metabolites, all of which are directed toward Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. These secondary metabolites, including 9-Hydroxy-12-oxo-10-octadecenoic acid, 6-Methoxymellein, and Isoscutellarein 8-O-glucoside, are known to target the same protein, which in turn is a known substrate of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ATR. The shared target of these compounds implies a possible mechanism of action involving the modulation of ATR activity through the regulation of Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. The evidence is consistent with a pathway where the primary compound may influence ATR through its interaction with the downstream target protein, suggesting a potential role in cellular processes regulated by ATR. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between the compound and ATR, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
